@startuml managed_agent_cli_flow
title Managed Agent CLI Runtime Flow

' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/cli/CampusClawCommand.java (call, createSession)
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentRuntimeManager.java (prepare, materialize)
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java (initialize, setAgentRuntime)
' Observed behavior: only the explicit CLI --agent-id path uses the CampusMate materializer.
' Architecture change: the public HTTP V1 runtime uses its own read-only .campusagent directory contract.

actor User
participant "CampusClawCommand" as CLI
participant "AgentRuntimeManager" as Runtime
participant "Local Agent Cache" as Cache
participant "CampusMateService" as Mate
participant "ToolCatalog" as Catalog
participant "AgentSession" as Session

User -> CLI: cli --agent-id agentId
CLI -> Runtime: prepare(agentId)
Runtime -> Cache: load complete .campusclaw snapshot

alt complete local snapshot
  Cache --> Runtime: PreparedAgentRuntime
else snapshot missing or unreadable
  Runtime -> Mate: GetAgentRuntime(agentId)
  Mate --> Runtime: Agent metadata and Skill coordinates
  loop each directly bound Skill
    Runtime -> Mate: querySkillInfo(skillId)
    Mate --> Runtime: Skill metadata and bound tools
  end
  Runtime -> Cache: materialize Agent and Skill files
  Runtime -> Cache: reload materialized snapshot
  Cache --> Runtime: PreparedAgentRuntime
end

Runtime --> CLI: prepared runtime
CLI -> Catalog: refresh(agentRoot)
CLI -> Session: setAgentRuntime(runtime, manager)
CLI -> Session: initialize(derived SessionConfig)
Session -> Cache: load system prompt and Skills
Session -> Catalog: resolve allowed local tools
Session --> User: interactive or one-shot CLI

note over CLI,Session
The HTTP V1 controllers do not enter this flow.
They read manager-provisioned .campusagent directories.
end note

@enduml
